[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and closed on 5 October. Its reports hold three
problems, and engineering closed two of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day moves are still open. Nothing in the parser fix or the form's retirement touches them: a
date that moves by one day is not a day/month swap. Keep #3 open and file new one-day reports there.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: { href: 'https://github.com/mr-hummel/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1', state: 'fixed' },
    hint: { href: 'https://github.com/mr-hummel/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2', state: "won't fix" },
    'one-day': { href: 'https://github.com/mr-hummel/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3', state: 'open' },
  }}
/>

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant writes the day
  first. Any date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped. Fixed:
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first,
  as told, and the form reads the date day first. Only the form at booking-v3 tenants does this.
  Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired.
- **`one-day`**: the reports the desk already read as a one-day move. A date moves by one day,
  not by a swap: one meeting on two days in two time zones, an invite sent before its booking.
  No fix yet.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
The subject says what people saw, a wrong day. It does not say why the day was wrong, so all three
problems arrived under the same subjects. Intake's tag does not separate them either: it
follows the reporter's browser, not the tenant.

## For the desk

- When a report is about a date, file it by tenant and channel, as [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)
  already shows, not by subject.
- A date off by one day is not a swap. File it with the one-day moves.
- A swapped date reported after 5 October means a fix did not hold. Open a new ticket for it and
  link #4471.
- The table above recounts #4471 from the data on every render.

